# evidence-for: AC-016, AC-017, FR-012
# evidence-timeout: 120
#
# GI-002, all three halves: the shipped asset, its first consumer, and the
# fact that the asset is actually INSTALLED where the run commits.
#
# Block 1 enumerates every git invocation the guard actually EXECUTES, with
# comment lines stripped — the header discusses the anti-pattern by name so a
# whole-file scan would flag the documentation. Every surviving query is an
# index query: --cached for the path list, :0:<path> blob reads for content.
# No stash, in any form. `rev-parse --verify HEAD` is a ref-existence check
# for the unborn-branch fallback, not a working-tree read.
#
# The D-014 shape lock is new this cycle. `git cat-file blob :0:$p | grep -q`
# FAILS OPEN above the pipe buffer: grep -q exits 0 on first match and closes
# the pipe, git dies of SIGPIPE (141), `pipefail` reports the pipeline as 141,
# and the enclosing `if` swallows that as "no match" — so the larger the
# violation the more reliably it committed. Measured: a 4.2 MB file with a
# conflict marker on line 1 committed cleanly. The guard now redirects each
# staged blob to a scratch file and checks the file, so the count of pipes on
# any `cat-file blob` line is the structural proof the shape is gone.
#
# Block 2 is the consumer half (A-034: run tooling, in scope; Pioneer PRODUCT
# code untouched). It lives in its own git repository at
# /Users/rayjanoka/ab/code/pioneer/.claude, so it cannot ride in this casting
# commit and is committed separately there.
#
# D-013 is the other half of "staged-only" that CAST got wrong. Converting the
# four path queries to --cached fixed WHICH FILES are judged; every check then
# still read "$PROJECT_ROOT/$file" — the WORKING TREE — so a peer's unstaged
# edit changed the verdict anyway. quality-gate.sh now checks the index out to
# a private temp tree (git checkout-index, ~0.4s on 3,565 files) and roots all
# thirteen judgments there. Zero linter or test invocations read PROJECT_ROOT.
#
# Block 3 answers PROVE's finding that the asset was shipped but never
# installed. GI-002 says the pioneer copy gets fixed "as a consumer of that
# asset", which requires the asset to be present. Both repositories the run
# commits to now carry it, byte-identical to the shipped source. Note the
# .claude repo is a SUBMODULE — its hook path resolves under
# .git/modules/.claude/hooks, which is exactly why the installer asks git
# (`rev-parse --git-path hooks`) instead of assuming .git/hooks.
#
# Block 4 matters as much as the query fix: the hook had NO Stop entry, so it
# never ran at all. A correct guard that is never invoked is not a guard.

